.nh
.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-ci - Audit the project for risky deps and exit non-zero on findings (one-stop CI command)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis ci [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
ci runs the full audit pipeline in one shot:
.IP "  1." 5
snapshot save     write aegis.lock from the live lockfile
.IP "  2." 5
snapshot enrich   AST-scan every dep (skip with --no-enrich)
.IP "  3." 5
score             apply allowlist + verdict thresholds
.IP "  4." 5
exit              0 = passed, 1 = findings, 2 = error

.PP
Designed to drop into a CI step:
.IP \(bu 2
run: aegis ci --fail-on=block
.IP \(bu 2
run: aegis ci --json | jq '.findings'

.PP
The fingerprint cache (~/.aegis/cache/fingerprints) persists across
runs, so a warm CI is fast — only newly-added or version-changed
deps incur AST scan cost.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--baseline\fP=""
	path to a saved aegis.lock to diff against (drift mode — catches version-changed deps that grew new capabilities; doesn't touch your aegis.lock)

.PP
\fB--fail-on\fP="block"
	verdict threshold to fail on: safe|review|prompt|block

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ci

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit a machine-readable JSON object to stdout (suppresses human output)

.PP
\fB--no-enrich\fP[=false]
	skip the AST scan; score only on existing fingerprints (faster but thinner)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only the summary line (no per-finding detail)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis(1)\fP
